WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm great. I'm great.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you?
-Good.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you just wrapped up
another season.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
How has it been doing
this show for the second time?

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Unbelievable. It really feels
like no time has passed.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so wonderful.
-It is.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:14.347
-And the fact you guys --
I mean, you obviously maintained

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
a friendship in all the time
it was off.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.451
But I can't imagine how nice it
is to spend that much time

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your friends again.
-I know.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we were off
for 12 1/2 years.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
So then --
-That's crazy.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's crazy!
So then to come back

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.562
and to be able to come and laugh
every single day together,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.530 line:92%
it really is just a gift.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you're --
you did that show,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
people might have thought,
you know,

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.669 size:84% position:42%
that was the first time
they got to know you.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you did shows before that.
-Yes.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your first show was
in 1995

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "Ned and Stacey."
-Yes.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:45.478 size:78% position:39%
-And how did that go?
-Um, it went okay.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.915 size:75% position:38%
I mean, it's a show.
That's hard to do.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a show.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.051 line:92%
-It was a show for two seasons.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.852 line:92%
I had just come from New York.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had never done
a TV show before.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.256 line:92%
And it was rolling along.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:00.660
And there was another show on
at the time called "Friends."

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was doing a little
better than us.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:05.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then one day the producers
come to me and they said,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:12.839
"Okay, the reason why 'Friends'
is so successful

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.376
is because of Jennifer Aniston's
hair."

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
These people worked in
television.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.114 line:92%
-And I was like, "Her hair?"

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:25.118
And they said, "Yes."
So, they brought her hairdresser

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
and made him cut my hair
into "The Rachel."

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, he -- you know,
he blew-dry it.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, it's 'The Rachel.'"

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the thing is,
he didn't teach anybody

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to blow-dry it.
And so, like,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's these -- you know,
we in the tribe,

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.703 size:75% position:38% line:92%
we call it Jew hair.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.805 line:92%
I had very, very curly hair.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're sitting there,
and they're like --

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
sweating trying to
straighten it.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.543 line:92%
And then they're quitting.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then another one
is trying to straighten it.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then that one quit.
Then another one.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Literally -- literally
three people quit

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.650 size:78% position:39%
because they couldn't
straighten my hair.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, "The Rachel,"
but, like, here's an example

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.955 line:92%
of this is your best effort.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:05.458 line:92%
-This is the best -- It worked.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's your "Rachel"
over there.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:12.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's like --

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like hair that's
dressing up like "The Rachel"

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.037 line:92%
to, like, get through security.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:22.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you notice
the mushroom-esque little --

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:27.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that was because
it literally, as I was acting,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it was growing.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.851 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.187
-And then, David Schwimmer
was on the show this year

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
playing your boyfriend.
-Yes.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.457
-Did you get a chance to tell
him that the reason "Friends"

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.459 size:88% position:44%
was successful because
of "The Rachel" haircut?

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't.
-Yeah, you should have.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-I think he would have been

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
really, really happy
to hear that.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.666
-Did you -- the first time you
did the show, because, again,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
you couldn't have expected it
was going to come back.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you take anything
from the set

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
after you wrapped
the first time?

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yes. The producer
said, you know,

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:55.808 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"What would you like?"

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.045
And I said that I wanted the
door from Grace Adler's Design.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I bet they thought
something smaller.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
-They did.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, okay.
-They did.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just wanted the door,
and just thought,

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, like, for art."
-Yeah.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, just lean it up
against a wall

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.992
and, you know, see if people
try to actually walk into it.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, that could be
kind of fun.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.063 line:92%
And, so, I brought it home.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:20.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next day, I got a call
from someone at NBC,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:25.305
and they said, "You owe us $25."
-$25?

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.473 line:92%
-And I said, "What? What?"

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"For the wood."

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Because they could have

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:34.914 size:75% position:38%
broken down the door
and used that wood

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for another pilot.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
So in order for me to keep
the door,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.689 line:92%
I had to pay $25 -- $250.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.991
-Oh, it was $250? Okay, got you.
-$250.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.460 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But I said, "Sue me."

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's, I think,
the right way to go.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.666 size:88% position:44%
Because, like, famously,
wood court is so long.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
It takes so long to get trial
in wood court.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure you would have
been fine.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think so.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it was, you know,
eight years.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
We made them $18 billion.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:06.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're saying,
"You have to pay me $250."

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, pbbbbbt!

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.815 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just picture,
there was, like,

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.417 size:84% position:42% line:92%
some carpenter came in.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like,
"Hey, where's the door?

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.521 line:92%
We were counting on that door!"

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:16.456 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"Go talk to Messing."

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. "I got to get my money
from Messing."

